Answer: As of September 16, 2020, the United States federal government had not announced any official plans, executive orders, or legislative proposals to mandate COVID-19 vaccination for all residents. The source explicitly argues against such a universal mandate, stating, "Universal mandates should not, at this point, be on the table," and notes significant logistical and legal barriers, including that "it is doubtful that the federal government has the authority to impose one."

