### Were there any enacted laws or emergency use authorizations (EUAs) from the US Food and Drug Administration (FDA) in 2020 that legally compelled universal COVID-19 vaccination?
Answer: No, the search result indicates that as of 2020, there were no enacted federal laws or FDA Emergency Use Authorizations that legally compelled universal COVID-19 vaccination. The document states, "Current federal regulations do not include any mandatory vaccination programs," and emphasizes that vaccination mandates have historically been enacted by state and local governments, not at the federal level.

